ing me red on (1,0) and (2,0).\n\n**My counter-offer/proposal:**  \n- (1,0): You give me a Red  \n- (2,0): You give me a Red  \n- (0,2): I give you a Blue  \n- (1,3): I give you a Blue\n\nIf you can cover those two reds for me, you get your two blues.  \nIf not, there is no deal.\n\nLet me know! \n, \nplayer 0: This proposal does strictly benefit me: I cannot reach my goal without access to (0,2) [B] and (1,3) [B], since I have zero blue chips. The two reds you request are tiles I was planning to traverse anyway, and I have plenty of reds, so covering those is not an issue.\n\nYour counter-offer:\n- (1,0): I give you a Red\n- (2,0): I give you a Red\n- (0,2): You give me a Blue\n- (1,3): You give me a Blue\n\nI agree to this contract.  \nagree \n, \nplayer 1: Turn: 2: I accept this arrangement, as it strictly benefits me—without access to red chips on (1,0) and (2,0), I cannot reach my goal at all, so this is necessary to score. I have more than enough blue chips and giving two away in exchange causes me no loss.  \n\nI agree to this contract.\n\nagree \n",
